                <pb facs="0377" n="273" sameAs="frus:frus1932v03/pg273"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/4129b: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Great Britain
                        (Atherton)</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-02-10T20:00:00-05:00">February 10, 1932—8
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>59. Department’s 56 February 6, 8 p.m. The following telegram has been received
                    from the American Consul General at Shanghai under date February 10, 9 p.m.</p>
                <p>[Here follows quotation of first three paragraphs of telegram No. 31, February
                    10, 1932, 9 p.m., printed on <ref target="#pg271">page 271</ref>.]</p>
                <p>Am informing Shanghai as follows:</p>
                <p>[Here follows quotation of main paragraph of telegram No. 13, February 10, 8
                    p.m., printed <hi rendition="#italic">supra.</hi>]</p>
                <p>Please inform the Foreign Office of the above. State to them that I perceive no
                    good ground for attempting at this time further communication with the Japanese
                    on this subject and no reason for any further delay by any Government or
                    organization in proceeding with any proposals or plan of action which it may
                    desire to propose or to act upon. This does not affect the suggestion which I
                    made to the British Ambassador yesterday for consideration in relation to
                    possible future action. Request that they inform Sir John Simon fully
                    immediately.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
